          "user_rubrik": "Is Mephzotheraphy better than micro-needling?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Mesotherapy is a cosmetic treatment that involves a series of microinjections into the middle layer of the skin (the mesoderm) to deliver a blend of vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients. It aims to rejuvenate the skin, improve hydration, and can target specific issues like pigmentation and scarring. The treatment is often considered more subtle and gradual compared to microneedling.\n\nMicroneedling, on the other hand, uses fine needles to create controlled micro-injuries in the skin, triggering the body's natural healing process and stimulating collagen and elastin production. This can lead to more immediate improvements in skin texture, tone, and the appearance of scars.\n\nIn summary, mesotherapy focuses on nutrient delivery for a gradual improvement, while microneedling is more about stimulating skin renewal and collagen production for more noticeable results. Given your concerns about dark spots and uneven tone, both treatments could be beneficial, but microneedling may offer quicker visible improvements.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0037-79-06507:1": 1.8817427158355713,
            "clueweb22-en0037-79-06507:2": 1.5932416915893555,
            "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:1": 0.9708782434463501,
            "clueweb22-en0041-58-07171:1": 0.7884198427200317,
            "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:1": 0.3074338138103485,
            "clueweb22-en0020-68-08676:4": 0.17583686113357544,
            "clueweb22-en0014-30-12480:9": 0.07891805469989777
          },
