  {
    "runtag": "genaius-summary-rewrite",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "6-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s clear, thanks! Now, could you explain what Mephzotheraphy is, and how it compares to microneedling for skin concerns like mine?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is Mephzotheraphy better than micro-needling?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Mesotherapy is a minimally invasive treatment that involves injecting a mixture of vitamins, enzymes, hormones, and plant extracts into the skin to rejuvenate and improve its appearance. It targets issues like uneven skin tone, dark spots, and visible pores by delivering nutrients directly to the skin\u2019s middle layer (mesoderm). This can stimulate collagen production, improve hydration, and enhance skin elasticity.\n\nCompared to microneedling, which creates micro-injuries to stimulate the skin\u2019s natural healing process and boost collagen, mesotherapy focuses more on delivering active ingredients to the skin. Microneedling is particularly effective for addressing enlarged pores, acne scars, and uneven texture, while mesotherapy is better suited for overall skin rejuvenation and hydration.\n\nFor your concerns\u2014dark spots, uneven tone, and visible pores\u2014microneedling might offer more targeted results, especially since it directly stimulates collagen and elastin production. However, mesotherapy could complement microneedling by providing hydration and nutrients to enhance your skin\u2019s overall health. Both treatments have minimal downtime, but it\u2019s essential to consult with a dermatologist to ensure the ingredients in mesotherapy are safe given your nut allergy.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0041-58-07171:0": 31.104400634765625
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.",
