      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about ways to make my skin look better besides using serums. Any ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I improve my skin's appearance except serums?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To enhance your skin's appearance, consider adopting healthy lifestyle habits such as eating a balanced diet, getting 7-8 hours of quality sleep, exercising regularly, managing stress, and protecting your skin from the sun, as these all contribute to a healthier complexion and can help reduce signs of aging and uneven tone [DOC-5]. Professional treatments like no-touch facials, exfoliating body treatments, and creams with ingredients like niacinamide and lactic acid can also improve skin texture and tone with minimal downtime [DOC-1]. For makeup, opt for oil-free foundations and concealers that help even out your complexion and minimize the appearance of pores, especially if you have sensitive skin or allergies [DOC-2]. These approaches, combined with your current skincare routine, can help you achieve smoother, more radiant skin. Do you want advice on nut-free skincare or makeup products?",
          "citations": {
