          "user_utterance": "Definitely! Redness is always a worry for me. Any recommendations for reducing it quickly? Also, can I use my hyaluronic acid in the days after, since that\u2019s already part of my routine?",
          "user_rubrik": "How does CO2 laser treatment work?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Redness after microneedling is common but usually fades within a few hours to a couple of days. To minimize it, apply a gentle, fragrance-free, nut-free moisturizer and pure hyaluronic acid, which is highly recommended for post-microneedling care and safe for sensitive skin and allergies [DOC-3][DOC-7]. Avoid sun exposure, makeup, and any harsh or fragranced products for at least 24-48 hours, and skip retinol, acids, and exfoliants for several days [DOC-1][DOC-7]. Using a physical sunscreen (not chemical) when you do go outside is also advised. If you experience flaking, continue with gentle moisturizers and avoid picking or scrubbing the skin [DOC-1][DOC-8]. Would you like recommendations for specific nut-free moisturizers or sunscreens?",
