          "text": "To choose a microneedling provider that aligns with your needs\u2014minimal downtime, nut allergy safety, and visible improvement in dark spots, uneven tone, and pores\u2014focus on these essentials:\n\n**1. Credentials & Experience**\n- Choose a board-certified dermatologist or licensed medical professional with specific experience in microneedling (especially for pigmentation and pores).\n- Ask about their experience with your skin type and concerns; microneedling is safe for most tones, but expertise matters for best results ([clueweb22-en0040-90-12567], [clueweb22-en0003-34-01095]).\n\n**2. Safety & Hygiene**\n- Ensure all equipment is sterilized and single-use needles are standard.\n- Confirm the clinic\u2019s protocols for allergy safety\u2014specifically, that no nut-derived products are used during or after your treatment ([clueweb22-en0000-42-05014]).\n\n**3. Technology & Customization**\n- Look for providers using advanced, FDA-cleared devices (e.g., MicroPen EVO, SkinPen) that",
