          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To enhance your microneedling results for dark spots, uneven tone, and visible pores\u2014while ensuring nut allergy safety and minimal downtime\u2014focus on these proven, well-tolerated ingredients and product types:\n\n**1. Hydration & Barrier Repair (First 2\u20133 Days)**\n- **Hyaluronic Acid:** Continue using pure, fragrance-free hyaluronic acid for deep hydration and barrier support. It\u2019s non-comedogenic and nut-free.\n- **Ceramides & Peptides:** Look for moisturizers with ceramides and peptides (e.g., IT Cosmetics Confidence in a Cream) to strengthen skin and speed recovery ([clueweb22-en0025-44-15240]).\n\n**2. Brightening & Texture Refinement (After 3\u20135 Days)**\n- **Vitamin C:** Resume your vitamin C routine to boost radiance and fade dark spots. Choose formulas free of nut oils and fragrances ([clueweb22-en0033-13-14792]).\n- **Retinol:** Retinol helps with cell turnover and pore refinement. Use a",
