          "user_utterance": "I'm curious about improving my skin's appearance. What are some options besides serums?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I improve my skin's appearance except serums?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To address your concerns\u2014dark spots, uneven tone, visible pores, nut allergies, makeup use, and a need for minimal downtime\u2014here are the most effective, non-serum options:\n\n**1. Professional Cosmetic Treatments (Minimal Downtime)**\n- **Facials with Steam & Extraction:** Opens pores, removes blackheads, and improves texture. Immediate results, but can be costly.\n- **Chemical Peels (Light/Medium):** Brighten dark spots, even tone, and refine pores. Downtime is usually minimal (mild redness/peeling for a few days). Always confirm nut-free formulations with your provider.\n\n**2. Topical Alternatives to Serums**\n- **Antibacterial Cover-Up Sticks or Powders:** Conceal imperfections while treating spots. Look for nut-free, antiseptic formulas.\n- **Moisturizers with SPF & Brightening Agents:** Products with zinc oxide, vitamin B5, and hyaluronic acid protect and hydrate, improving dullness and uneven tone. These are generally well-tolerated and available in nut-free options.\n\n**3.",
