          "user_utterance": "Thank you for the details! If I wanted to try microneedling, how often should I schedule the sessions for best results?",
          "user_rubrik": "How does CO2 laser treatment work?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For best results with microneedling\u2014especially to address dark spots, uneven tone, and visible pores with minimal downtime\u2014most dermatologists recommend:\n\n- **Frequency:** 3 sessions, each spaced about 1 month apart. This schedule allows your skin to heal and maximize collagen production between treatments.\n- **Results Timeline:** Noticeable improvement after each session, with optimal glow and texture by the third treatment. Results continue to improve for months as collagen builds.\n- **Maintenance:** After your initial series, a yearly maintenance session helps prolong benefits.\n- **Suitability:** Microneedling (including radiofrequency microneedling) is safe for most skin tones and has minimal downtime\u2014usually just 1\u20132 days of mild redness. It\u2019s also generally safe for those with nut allergies, but always confirm nut-free post-care products.\n\nWould you like tips on choosing a provider or advice on post-treatment care to maximize results and safety?",
