          "user_rubrik_score": 1,
          "text": "To enhance your microneedling results\u2014targeting dark spots, uneven tone, and visible pores, while respecting your nut allergy and need for minimal downtime\u2014here\u2019s how to safely incorporate special products and treatments:\n\n**1. Hydration & Barrier Support (First 2\u20133 Days)**\n- Stick to gentle, fragrance-free moisturizers and pure hyaluronic acid for hydration. This supports healing and is safe for nut allergies ([clueweb22-en0009-89-01915]).\n- Avoid actives (vitamin C, retinol, AHAs/BHAs) for at least 2\u20133 days post-treatment to prevent irritation, as microneedling dramatically increases product absorption ([clueweb22-en0009-89-01915]).\n\n**2. Brightening & Texture Improvement (After 3\u20135 Days)**\n- Once skin has calmed, resume your vitamin C and retinol routine to boost collagen and fade dark spots. These are proven to enhance microneedling outcomes ([clueweb22-en0042-13-06743]).",
