          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "These ingredient suggestions are really helpful! Are there any treatments or products I should avoid entirely after microneedling?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is Mephzotheraphy better than micro-needling?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 1,
          "text": "Absolutely\u2014here\u2019s what you should avoid after microneedling, tailored to your nut allergy, makeup use, and desire for minimal downtime and visible improvement:\n\n**Products & Treatments to Avoid Post-Microneedling**\n\n- **Strong Exfoliants:** No AHA/BHA acids (glycolic, lactic, mandelic, salicylic) for at least 2\u20133 days post-treatment. These can cause irritation and disrupt healing ([clueweb22-en0033-70-02855], [clueweb22-en0023-06-19151], [clueweb22-en0009-89-01915]).\n- **Retinol & Vitamin C:** Pause both for 2\u20133 days after microneedling\u2014even if you use them daily\u2014since increased absorption can lead to sensitivity ([clueweb22-en0033-70-02855], [clueweb22-en0023-06-19151]).\n- **Makeup:** Wait at least 24 hours before applying makeup to avoid clogging open microchannels ([cl",
