    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for ways to improve my skin\u2019s appearance besides serums. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I improve my skin's appearance except serums?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You may want to consider incorporating a moisturizer into your routine. A good moisturizer can help to hydrate and nourish your skin, leaving it looking smoother and more even-toned. Look for a moisturizer that is formulated for your skin type and contains ingredients that address your specific concerns, such as dark spots or uneven tone. You may also want to consider using a facial oil or cream that contains antioxidants and other beneficial ingredients. Additionally, don't forget to protect your skin from the sun by using a broad-spectrum sunscreen with at least SPF 30 every day. Get enough sleep and try to reduce your screen time to help your skin look its best. Consider using a humidifier in your home to add moisture to the air, which can help to improve the appearance of your skin. Lastly, be gentle with your skin and avoid using harsh products or exfoliating too frequently, as this can cause irritation and dryness. By incorporating these tips into your routine, you may see an improvement",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0040-40-08298:16": 2.5392208099365234,
            "clueweb22-en0038-70-01668:19": 2.4411728382110596,
            "clueweb22-en0037-99-06685:0": 1.7689948081970215,
