          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019ve heard CO2 laser treatments can be pretty intensive. Can you explain exactly how a CO2 laser works on the skin?",
          "user_rubrik": "How does CO2 laser treatment work?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A CO2 laser works by delivering an intense wavelength of light to the skin, which removes the outer layers of aged or sun-damaged skin. In addition, the laser stimulates the underlying skin, resulting in collagen formation and an improvement in wrinkles. As the lasered skin heals following the procedure, new skin forms that are smoother and tighter. The laser removes surface cells of the epidermis, making way for fresh, clear new skin. At the same time, it penetrates the skin's deeper dermis layer to stimulate new collagen production, which firms and smooths skin over time. This process can help to address a range of concerns, including fine lines and wrinkles, discoloration, acne scars, stretch marks, and uneven skin texture. The laser can also treat benign skin growths like warts and birthmarks, as well as some skin cancers. The skin condition rhinophyma, which increases skin thickness on the nose, also responds well to CO2 laser treatment. The",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:1": 5.277205944061279,
            "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:2": 3.462416410446167,
            "clueweb22-en0020-47-00301:9": 3.05094575881958,
            "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:4": 2.627426862716675,
            "clueweb22-en0040-90-08092:8": 2.3838839530944824
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that clears up a lot. How is a fractional treatment different from an ablative one?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the difference between fractional and blative treatments?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A fractional CO2 laser treatment is different from an ablative one in that it delivers a partial beam of light that targets only a fraction of the skin, in a pixelated pattern. This means that only some skin is removed, making the treatment less aggressive and less painful compared to an ablative laser. Ablative lasers, on the other hand, completely remove the outer layers of skin, which can be more intense and require more downtime. Fractional treatments are usually better for surface-level improvement and can be adjusted to suit individual skin concerns, whereas ablative treatments are more effective for deeper skin issues but come with a higher risk of side effects. The downtime for fractional treatments is also typically shorter, ranging from a few days to a week, whereas ablative treatments can require a minimum of two weeks of downtime. Overall, fractional treatments are a good option for those who want to improve their skin with minimal downtime and risk.  Best Acne Treatment - When pores are clogged with dirt and oil",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:10": 4.948027610778809,
            "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:12": 3.4362893104553223,
