      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "How exactly does CO2 laser treatment work? Is it painful?",
          "user_rubrik": "How does CO2 laser treatment work?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "CO2 laser treatment works by delivering concentrated light beams that target water molecules in the skin, vaporizing damaged surface cells and stimulating new collagen production in deeper layers. This process removes old skin, allowing new, smoother, and tighter skin to form. Fractional CO2 lasers create tiny, pixelated channels, which promotes faster healing and reduced downtime. This helps address concerns like visible pores, dark spots, and uneven tone.\n\nRegarding pain, CO2 laser resurfacing is typically performed with anesthesia, often topical numbing cream, to ensure minimal discomfort during the procedure. More aggressive treatments might use local anesthetic. Post-operative pain is usually minimal and manageable with oral painkillers. Newer fractional CO2 lasers are known for minimized pain.",
          "citations": {
