        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What\u2019s the difference between fractional and ablative treatments?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the difference between fractional and blative treatments?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Fully ablative CO2 lasers remove the entire top layer of skin in the treated area, leading to more intense results, longer downtime (weeks), and often requiring general anesthesia. In contrast, fractional CO2 lasers treat only a fraction of the skin in a pixelated pattern, creating microscopic columns of treated tissue while leaving surrounding skin untouched. This allows for faster healing (days of downtime) and reduced risks, though typically requiring multiple sessions for desired results. Fractional is a delivery method that can be applied to ablative lasers.",
