      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really specific, thank you! How long does the redness and peeling usually last after microneedling?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the side effects of CO2 laser, microneedling, chemical peeling, and microdermabrasion?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "After microneedling, redness typically subsides significantly within 12 to 48 hours, though it can persist for a few days, potentially up to 3-4 days, or even a week. Peeling or flaking usually begins 3 to 5 days post-treatment and can continue for up to a week as your skin undergoes cell turnover. The duration can vary based on the aggressiveness of the treatment and individual healing.",
