        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m just curious\u2014are there any good ways to improve my skin\u2019s appearance besides using serums?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I improve my skin's appearance except serums?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Beyond serums, several non-serum methods can improve your skin. Consider incorporating **topical retinoid or retinol creams**, which boost collagen, reduce pore size, fade dark spots, and improve fine lines (P4, P5, P10, P12, P15). Start gradually due to potential sensitivity and always use sunscreen. **BHA (Salicylic Acid) liquids or creams** are excellent exfoliants for unclogging pores, brightening, and evening skin tone (P1, P10, P12). Products with **Niacinamide (Vitamin B3)** can enhance brightness, reduce dark spots, and strengthen your skin barrier (P5, P12). Look for **moisturizers or night creams** specifically formulated to brighten dullness and even tone, which can also address signs of poor sleep (P9, P20). Daily **sun protection** with zinc oxide is also crucial for preventing dark spots (P5).",
          "citations": {
