        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks. Can you tell me more about the microneedling side effects specifically?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the side effects of CO2 laser, microneedling, chemical peeling, and microdermabrasion?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Microneedling can cause several temporary side effects, including short-term swelling, redness, skin flaking, peeling, bruising, bleeding, and inflammation. You might also experience itching, stinging, or a tingling sensation, and your skin may feel drier. It's important to note that skin will be more sun-sensitive after treatment, and microneedling may worsen active breakouts or stimulate cold sores if you have a history of oral herpes. Bacterial infection is also a potential risk.",
