      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What\u2019s the main difference between \u201cablative\u201d and \u201cfractional\u201d treatments then?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the difference between fractional and blative treatments?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The main difference between ablative and fractional CO2 laser treatments lies in how much skin they treat. Fully ablative CO2 lasers remove the entire top layer of the skin, leading to more dramatic results but requiring intense treatments, often general anesthesia, and a longer recovery time (weeks). In contrast, fractional CO2 lasers treat only a fraction of the skin in a pixelated pattern, leaving surrounding skin untouched. This approach is less aggressive, results in shorter downtime (days), but typically requires a series of sessions for optimal results.",
          "citations": {
