      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I see! Is Mephzotheraphy actually better than microneedling for pigmentation and pores?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is Mephzotheraphy better than micro-needling?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Both microneedling and mesotherapy can address pigmentation and visible pores, but they work differently. Microneedling creates micro-injuries to stimulate collagen and elastin, reducing pore size and improving pigmentation. It also enhances the absorption of topical skin-brightening agents. Mesotherapy, on the other hand, involves injecting a customized blend of vitamins, hyaluronic acid, and other nutrients directly into the skin, with specific formulations targeting pigmentation by controlling melanin production. While microneedling is based on the concept of mesotherapy, the key difference lies in the direct injection of substances in mesotherapy versus the skin's natural healing and topical absorption enhancement in microneedling. The effectiveness can vary based on the specific concerns and individual response.",
