        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually looking for ways to improve my skin\u2019s appearance without relying just on serums. Any advice?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I improve my skin's appearance except serums?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To improve your skin without relying solely on serums, consider incorporating creams with ingredients like Retinol, Niacinamide (Vitamin B3), or collagen to address pores, dark spots, and uneven tone. Washes containing charcoal, witch hazel, or salicylic acid can help with visible pores. For natural options, explore DIY masks with baking soda and apple cider vinegar or lemon juice, or use buttermilk. Always apply a non-comedogenic broad-spectrum sunscreen daily. You can also add L-Ascorbic Acid powder to your existing creams for brightening.",
