      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s interesting! How does CO2 laser treatment actually work?",
          "user_rubrik": "How does CO2 laser treatment work?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "CO2 laser treatment works by delivering concentrated light beams that vaporize damaged surface skin cells (epidermis) and heat the underlying dermis. This process removes outer layers of aged or sun-damaged skin, while stimulating new collagen production. As the skin heals, it becomes smoother, tighter, and more even-toned. This mechanism effectively addresses concerns like visible pores, dark spots, and uneven texture by revealing fresh skin and improving overall skin structure.",
