      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps, thanks! Is Mephzotheraphy better than micro-needling?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is Mephzotheraphy better than micro-needling?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Mesotherapy and microneedling differ in their approach. Microneedling creates microscopic punctures to stimulate your skin's natural collagen and elastin production, addressing concerns like scars, wrinkles, pores, and pigmentation. It typically has minimal downtime with temporary redness and swelling. Mesotherapy, on the other hand, involves injecting vitamins and anti-aging substances directly into the skin to stimulate regeneration, reduce fine lines, and reverse sun damage. It also offers lesser downtime. The \"better\" option depends on your specific skin concerns and desired outcomes.",
