    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually looking for ideas to improve my skin\u2019s appearance besides using serums. What would you suggest?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I improve my skin's appearance except serums?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great \u2014 here are practical, non - serum steps to boost appearance : - review timing : use vitamin c in the morning and move retinol to the evening ( retinol works best at night and combining both in am can increase irritation ). - sunscreen every morning ( broad \u2011 spectrum mineral spf ) \u2014 essential for preventing dark spots and protecting retinol results. - add targeted actives in other product forms : a bha pore \u2011 minimizing toner for visible pores ( daily ), a glycolic or lactic acid mask / peel once weekly to resurface and fade spots. - layer a lightweight oil ( squalane or vitamin c rose oil ) after moisturizer to lock hydration \u2014 1 \u2013 2 drops or mixed into foundation for a dewy finish ; if oily, mist first. - dedicated eye cream and occlusive moisturizer at night to improve texture and fine lines. - in \u2011 office options with minimal downtime : mild chemical peels, microdermabrasion, or ipl for pigmentation ( consult a dermatologist ). - lifestyle : prioritize sleep, hydrate, limit direct screen glare, and avoid nut - containing skin",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0004-09-10237:6": -0.0515555813908577,
            "clueweb22-en0025-03-00252:0": -0.08980543911457062,
